# Committed. Placeholders only — never a real value. Prime directive 16.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and holds the real values locally. A copy of every real secret also
# lives in the vault named in docs/SECRETS.md, so keeping it out of git never loses it.
#
# Keep the key set here identical to the key set in `.env`. A key that exists only in one
# person's `.env` is a key the next session will not know to ask for.

# --- Secrets. Real values live in .env (local) and the vault; nothing in GitHub.
{{SECRET_NAME}}=replace-me
DATABASE_URL=replace-me

# --- Not secrets. These identify the project and may be committed; they are here so a fresh
# --- clone sees the whole configuration surface in one place. See docs/SECRETS.md.
APP_ENV=development
